WEBVTT

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.559
Here's Gem Island, the starter game,

00:00:05.559 --> 00:00:06.947
with a few things of my own:

00:00:06.987 --> 00:00:09.350
trees, rocks and a stack of crates.

00:00:09.437 --> 00:00:11.986
To start new games from it, save it as a template.

00:00:12.026 --> 00:00:14.006
Open the GameStudio menu.

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:16.303
Choose Save as Template.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.684
The Id is the template's folder name:

00:00:19.725 --> 00:00:22.308
lowercase, with dashes for spaces.

00:00:22.867 --> 00:00:25.491
The Label is its name in the New Project list:

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:26.646
My Island.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.422
And the Description is the one line shown beside it.

00:00:31.233 --> 00:00:33.044
It's saved in your Documents folder,

00:00:33.044 --> 00:00:34.989
under GameStudio, Templates.

00:00:35.029 --> 00:00:36.272
Click Save Template.

00:00:36.272 --> 00:00:38.403
Your game itself stays as it is.

00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:40.889
The status bar says it's saved.

00:00:40.976 --> 00:00:42.485
Now start a new game from it:

00:00:42.485 --> 00:00:44.836
open the GameStudio menu again.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.904
Choose New Project.

00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:50.585
Your template is here, under Your templates,

00:00:50.585 --> 00:00:51.944
after the built-in ones.

00:00:51.944 --> 00:00:52.902
Pick it.

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:54.814
Give the new game a name:

00:00:54.814 --> 00:00:55.993
Crystal Cove.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.279
Click Create.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.214
GameStudio copies your template

00:01:02.214 --> 00:01:03.973
into a new folder and sets it up.

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:05.587
It takes a few seconds.

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:09.139
Crystal Cove opens with everything from your template:

00:01:09.139 --> 00:01:11.241
the trees, the rocks and the crates,

00:01:11.241 --> 00:01:13.406
with the starter's player and gems.

00:01:13.446 --> 00:01:14.439
Click a tree.

00:01:14.445 --> 00:01:16.123
It's part of the new game.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.370
And the Game Project panel shows it's Crystal Cove,

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:21.072
a new game in its own folder.

00:01:21.077 --> 00:01:23.359
Gem Island stays as it was.

00:01:23.933 --> 00:01:25.495
That's your own template.

00:01:25.582 --> 00:01:27.312
Every new game can start from it,

00:01:27.312 --> 00:01:30.313
with its levels, its code and its custom skills.
